Name: livesplit
Author: Alex Vu
Date: 8/26/26

Description:
A livesplit mac menu bar to keep me productive. ironically, the time I spent 
making this could've been used more effectively to actually be productive.

Running:
  .venv/bin/python setup.py py2app -A
  open dist/livesplit.app

Notes:
  -A is an alias build: it symlinks the source, so edits take effect on the
  next `open` with no rebuild. Drop -A for a real standalone bundle.

  The .app is named after CFBundleName in setup.py, NOT the script filename.
  APP = ['livesplit.py'] + CFBundleName 'livesplit' -> dist/livesplit.app

  Don't change CFBundleIdentifier (com.alexvu.livesplit). macOS ties the
  notification permission to that ID; a new one means re-approving.